# The same modem and the same Cisco at 1200 bit/s, so the pair of them
# say something the boards cannot: what changes across a rate is the
# modulation and not the far end.  The banner is the same text through
# 300 baud FSK and through 600 baud DPSK.
#
# That is also all the checking this one has had, and it is worth being
# plain about the difference.  The 300 bit/s fixture beside it is
# confirmed byte for byte by minimodem; there is no second V.22 receiver
# to hand, so what stands behind these expect: lines is that a different
# modulation, a different receiver in this same program, and a
# separately recorded call return the text minimodem confirmed on the
# other one.  Strong, and not independent.
source:    recordings/third-party/netcomm-2400sa-1200bps.wav, left channel
seconds:   27.0
role:      originate
modes:     v22,v22bis
v8:        no
connect:   V22 1200
expect:    User Access Verification
expect:    Username:
tolerance: 0
